From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a thread's hook count never goes below zero, and never ends the server

add_queue_hook_count asserted that a thread's count of global hooks stays at
zero or above. In a shared prefix the server is the machine's Windows system,
so the assertion ended every Windows program of every user and every service
at once. It fired when a remote-support helper's 32-bit hook loader (TightVNC's
hookldr.exe, which sets global hooks on the helper's desktop) ended: removing
its hooks decremented a thread on that desktop that had never been counted for
them (remove_hook walks the desktop's threads). A count that would go below
zero now stays at zero, and the server says so once on stderr. A zero count
only makes that thread skip a hook call it would otherwise have made.

The imbalance itself is not found yet (left in the remote-support notes).

Gate: sg-session's test/remote-support-gate.sh (a VNC viewer connected and
disconnected; before, the machine's server aborted each time).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_HOOK_COUNT_ASSERT.
---
--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -701,6 +701,22 @@
     SHARED_WRITE_BEGIN( thread->queue->shared, queue_shm_t )
     {
         shared->hooks_count[index] += count;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HOOK_COUNT_ASSERT
+        /* Stained Glass OS (9628): a count that would go below zero stays at
+         * zero. This server is the machine's: an assertion here ended every
+         * Windows program of every user and every service at once -- it fired
+         * when a remote-support helper's 32-bit hook loader (TightVNC's
+         * hookldr.exe, global hooks) ended, decrementing a thread on its
+         * desktop that had never been counted for that hook. A zero count
+         * only makes that thread skip the hook call it would have made. */
+        if (shared->hooks_count[index] < 0)
+        {
+            static int told;
+            if (!told++) fprintf( stderr, "wineserver: hook count of thread %04x below zero (hook %u); kept at 0\n",
+                                  thread->id, index );
+            shared->hooks_count[index] = 0;
+        }
+#endif
     }
     SHARED_WRITE_END;
 
